+`0029-plugin-gl-attributes-by-name.patch` fixes plugin vertex attributes on
+OpenGL. A plugin program's attribute list leaves out the attributes of
+properties bound as uniforms, but the program indexed that list by each active
+attribute's linked location, so a data-driven attribute declared after a
+uniform-bound one received the wrong id or none. The program now matches active
+attributes to declared ones by name, which also makes explicit
+`layout(location = N)` optional on OpenGL; built-in shaders, whose lists are in
+location order, behave as before. The patch adds the first rendering tests that
+draw data-driven plugin paint attributes, on every backend: a packed composite
+scalar at a fractional zoom, a packed float2, a color pair, a feature-state
+refill of one feature, and two segments in one drawable, beside a camera-only
+property whose attribute leaves the program. It also corrects a test guard that
+tested whether the always-defined uniform macro was defined. This patch is not
+yet proposed upstream.
+
 Each patch is the squashed diff of its upstream branch, applied on top of the
 patches before it, so a patch that adds a test next to an earlier patch's test
 carries that placement rather than the branch's own context.
